WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:07.440
Post-processing effects enable you to define the overall look and feel of your scene through

2
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:13.359
various properties and features that affect coloring, tone mapping, lighting, and more.

3
00:00:13.359 --> 00:00:17.940
We use a special type of volume called a post-processing volume that can be added

4
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.719
to the level to access these features.

5
00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:25.879
Take note, you can add multiple volumes in your level to define the look of a specific

6
00:00:25.879 --> 00:00:30.640
area or layer effects for finer granular control.

7
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:36.259
So if we jump back to our scene, now real quick, I've opened the Lit Atmos In class,

8
00:00:36.259 --> 00:00:42.100
and if you're following along or you didn't save, all I simply did is go up to our window,

9
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.320
I went to our Environment Light Mixer, click through all of our properties, and then

10
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.000
for our Environment Height Fog, I made sure the volumetric fog was checked.

11
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.619
And of course then we put them in a folder just called Environment, and you can see

12
00:00:54.619 --> 00:00:56.179
all of these actors.

13
00:00:56.179 --> 00:01:00.840
And then holding Ctrl L, just simply adjust your light where you want.

14
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.099
So I'll do something over here, and we're ready to go.

15
00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:09.439
The next step that we want to do is, in this level, we already have a post-processing

16
00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:10.439
volume.

