00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:46.849
It is a brush, so we can actually adjust the individual, essentially, vertices of this,

26
00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:51.969
or we can change the shape to something like a cylinder, a sphere, a capsule.

27
00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:53.290
We're going to keep it as a cube.

28
00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.189
That's absolutely fine for right now.

29
00:01:55.189 --> 00:02:00.230
But what I want to make note of is that the settings that this post-processing volume

30
00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:06.510
is going to change or implement, which is what's in the Details panel here, by default

31
00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.050
is set to be only within that volume.

32
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:13.189
So the camera that we're viewing through, so if I move the camera around here, once

33
00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:18.909
it enters into this space, that's when these settings will be applied.

34
00:02:18.949 --> 00:02:23.729
Now for this one, we actually want the settings to be applied across our whole scene, and

35
00:02:23.729 --> 00:02:25.930
ignore the shape.

