45
00:03:00.449 --> 00:03:02.129
you have priority set up.

46
00:03:02.129 --> 00:03:04.169
So zero is going to be our default.

47
00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:10.210
So say that I want to use this base post-processing volume to just set up my exposure, maybe disable

48
00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:16.210
some effects, whatever, just establish essentially a baseline, I would just keep this as zero.

49
00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:23.129
I could then add another post-processing volume, and by simply checking any one of these properties,

50
00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:26.590
it's going to override whatever is below that.

51
00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:30.689
So by setting my priority just higher than whatever the previous ones, anything I change

52
00:03:30.689 --> 00:03:31.990
will override that.

53
00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.189
Hopefully that makes sense.

54
00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:37.389
Now for this example, we just need one post-processing volume, and we're going to

55
00:03:37.389 --> 00:03:38.419
start there.

56
00:03:38.419 --> 00:03:43.379
All right, so with our Infinite Extent Unbound checked, I'm going to scroll back up, and

